WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.129
Foreign keys also need a decision about

00:00:02.155 --> 00:00:03.826
what happens when a parent row is

00:00:03.839 --> 00:00:07.964
deleted RESTRICT or NO ACTION blocks the

00:00:07.977 --> 00:00:11.559
deletion while dependent child rows exist This

00:00:11.572 --> 00:00:13.730
is often appropriate for master data such

00:00:13.743 --> 00:00:16.309
as patients providers or services that are

00:00:16.335 --> 00:00:21.809
referenced by historical activity CASCADE
automatically removes

00:00:21.836 --> 00:00:25.220
dependent child rows That can be appropriate

00:00:25.246 --> 00:00:26.970
when the child has no meaning without

00:00:26.983 --> 00:00:29.404
the parent such as appointment service lines

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:33.300
when the appointment itself is deleted SET

00:00:33.326 --> 00:00:35.142
NULL keeps the child but removes the

00:00:35.155 --> 00:00:37.168
reference which only makes sense when the

00:00:37.181 --> 00:00:41.505
relationship is optional Do not choose CASCADE

00:00:41.531 --> 00:00:44.626
simply because it is convenient Choose the

00:00:44.639 --> 00:00:46.903
referential action based on the real meaning

00:00:46.929 --> 00:00:49.403
and retention requirements of the relationship
